The  driver provides support for the newer (post 1997) ICP‐Vortex
GDT and Intel Storage RAID controllers.  The driver provides  ac‐
cess  to  logical  devices  (disk  arrays)  presented by the con‐
troller.  The driver provides direct access to other SCSI devices
attached to the controller, such as tape or CD‐ROM drives.   This
message  may  be  displayed  during autoconfiguration if the con‐
troller’s memory is mapped below 1MB in physical  address  space.
This  can  be  disabled  either through changing a setting in the
controller’s BIOS utility, or changing the position of  a  jumper
on  the  board.  See your controller’s documentation for more in‐
formation.  The driver first appeared in and was based on the and
drivers of the same name.  ISA & EISA front‐ends and a management
interface are needed.  Older PCI boards are not yet supported.
